dsv41 patch 0036: backport of vLLM #54951 + fix #61647: split the prefill rows of the replicated sparse indexer across
the TP ranks (cost-balanced contiguous row slices against the full key history; an all_gatherv of the int32 top-k restores
the order). Same kernels per row. Base: the pin's sparse_attn_indexer.py and indexer.py incl. our 0033.
Threshold via VLLM_INDEXER_TP_SHARD_MIN_ROWS (default 65536 = off at max-num-batched-tokens 4096; we use 2048). Layers 20
and 24/28/32/36 stay replicated (candidate source/readers), so layers 2/8/14 are split. Unit tests 12/12 on GB10.

